      "writtenOn": "2024-10-10T21:23:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Brox did not stuff the battery presence GPIO.  So the `wakeup_battery()` call keeps running until `PRECHARGE_TIMEOUT_US` expires (30 seconds).\n\nIf we don\u0027t know the battery state, I think the charge manager should skip any changes to the charge port to avoid losing power.\n\nI think we might hit the same scenario when exiting battery cutoff.  There could be a period of time where the battery hasn\u0027t woken up, but the charger manager is fully seeded and tries to switch the charging port.\n\nThis is a corner case, as it means a user connected multiple chargers to the chromebook to exit battery cut-off.",
